  "created": "2022-03-17T13:26:50.083Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Covering a bone is a common use case of capsule collider. Currently, to do this, we must adjust not only the height but also position. So I think it will be nice to have \"hemisphere centered editing option\" in VRCPhysBoneCollider editor.\nI imagine that while this option is enabled, it treats the position vector value of the capsule (that the inspector displays) as if the local origin is at the center of the hemisphere's base. Then, we can easily cover the bone by only adjusting the height. (see attached 1st image)\nAdditionally, it might be useful to have \"adjust height\" operation. It adjusts the height so that the another hemisphere center matches child transform (i.e. bone's tail).\nThis option is not only for the height, it will also help rotation adjustments.  (see attached 2nd image)",
